believe:
That entire death shall null my entire thought;
And I feel torture, not that I believe thee,
But that I cannot disbelieve thee not.

bells:
And fled on southward in the roar of steam.
The marriage-bells of Romney must be loud,
To sound so clear through all! I was not well;

believing:
Which must, I know, yet be the corner-stone
Of all believing,--birds now flying fearless
Across would drop in terror to the earth;

beloved:
All blent in one yet each one manifest;
Each one distinguished and beloved as well
As if no second voice in earth or heaven

belated:
No squirrel went abroad;
A dog's belated feet
Like intermittent plush were heard

bellows:
First he piled on resinous wood,
Next plied the bellows in hopeful mood;
Thinking, 'My love and I will live.

belov'd:
Of rough, uneasy wilderness, poor lamb,
Poor child, poor child?—Aurora, my belov’d,
I will not vex you any more to-night;

belted:
Paris could not lay the fold
Belted down with emerald;
Venice could not show a cheek

belshazzar's:
He never had but one;
Belshazzar's correspondent
Concluded and begun

belles:
Comme l'amour, comme la mort;
Et j'ai fait les plus belles de belle argile
Sèche et fragile.

belov:
Still mock me with a name;
My best belovèd die
And I cannot die with them.

belfair:
And yet a revelation in some sort:
That’s hard, my critic Belfair! So—what next?
My critic Stokes objects to abstract thoughts;

belmore:
Such delicate perspectives of full life;
Nor Belmore, for the unity of aim
To which he cuts his cedarn poems, fine

belike:
Not much worse off in being fatherless
Than I was, fathered. He will say, belike,
His mother was the saddest creature born;
